Z||000005||88formula||05-30-2001||07:49 PM|||| It should be close to 0-60 in 8.7 seconds and the quarter mile in 16.6 seconds @ 85.8 mph.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||kslish||05-30-2001||11:42 PM||||My '87 GT is about the same as yours, and I know mine is sick (like you, I just haven't figured out what).  I'm already saving up for a rebuild.  When I first got it, it ran 0-60 in 12.5 seconds, and after replacing a lot of tune up items (plugs, filters, etc. etc.) I got it down to 11.0 seconds.  My slightly modded 4cyl Fiero can outrun it.  I'm rapidly coming to the conclusion that the previous owner didn't do ANY routine maintenance.  Compression check is next I guess.  Is yours setting any engine trouble codes?  Mine isn't and I'm hesitant to just start throwing parts at it.  The engine is just an absolute dog between 2000-3000 rpm then it finally has some get up and go.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||05-31-2001||12:02 AM||||Mine has some power. It can toast just about any other kids cars in town, even some 350 chevy's. I think its got tons of power. The other day I was seeing what kind of top speed it could do, and had it up to about 117 mph, and the check engine light came on and the engine started messin' with me. Checked codes and it said somthing like the EGR valve wasn't close with so much vaccum or somthing, I can't remember. But other then that, no I don't get any abnormal codes, other then my idle being too high, and my damn MAP sensor comming unplugged all the time. Anyone think this could be TPS related? Or IAC?||||reg||1
Z||000008||SPDFREK||05-31-2001||12:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>Yeap, my thoughts excatly. My parents 460 SEFI towncar will kick the crapp outta me, and it can only keep up with my 3.4 GT. Any off the top guesses about what could be wrong. Ask me anything! I put new head gaskets on about 3500 miles ago. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Have to checked your fuel Pressure with an external gauge? I Know a lot of people check that last, but it's been my exp that that's usually the first thing to degrade performance.<P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
