Z||000012||Black88GT||05-31-2001||12:37 PM||||Stopwatch is never accurate.  Its best to use a Gtec if you don't have a local track or don't want to go.  <P>Probably have a leaky injector.  Check vacuum lines also or EGR tube.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||05-31-2001||01:09 PM||||If your speedo is accurate you can get to within a half second timing yourself from 0 to 60. You'll be in the ballpark at least.<P>When the 2.8L V6 first came out, road and track or one of those mags tested it, and reported it could do 8.4 or 8.6S for 0 to 60.<P> Mine, with the auto tranny, is completely stock, and last time I tried it I did about 8.9 S.<P>  0 to 60 is a pretty good quick test of how your drive train is running. How it feels from day to day is subjective, but when you click the stop watch, and if you time yourself the same way everytime, you get a solid check on how well your car is in tune.<P>  running a quarter mile is not as easy - can get yourself into legal trouble real quick - and the cops arnt interested in how you changed your timing 2 degrees and need to know how it effects the HP.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Carrolles||05-31-2001||02:01 PM||||85SE v-6 4spd<BR>Grooms rebuilt stock 2.8L long block (about 10000 miles ago)<BR>ported intake and exhaust manifolds<BR>new clutch (stock Borg Warner OEM)<BR>BF Goodrich T/A 215-60R14 tires<BR>Everything else is bone stock<P>G-Tech results<BR>7.98 0 to 60 mph<BR>15.7 sec quarter mile at 87.7 mph<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jefrysuko||05-31-2001||03:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>and my damn MAP sensor comming unplugged all the time.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When you say coming unplugged do you mean the electrical connection or the vacuum line?  If it is vacuum then you might want to look into your catalytic converter being clogged.  This would also account for your slow 0-60 times.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Alex4mula||05-31-2001||03:24 PM||||Launch is very critical at least with stick. 300-500rpm up or down can easily make a 0.3s difference.<BR>I have Brooklands book with all the Fiero magazine articles (R&T, Car Driver, etc). 0-60 times quoted varies from 7.7 (lowest) to 8.6. All of them on V6 stick car.<p>[This message has been edited by Alex4mula (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
